ew cooperation concerns. Also B has excellent computer skills, good at assessing weather, handles stress well, very conscientious. Also B can be grumpy. So we might argue that the crew cooperation issue is more serious than Agent 2 suggests, and perhaps Candidate C's calmness and decision quality outweigh B's cooperation concerns. Or we could argue that B's reliability and stress handling are critical, and the cooperation issue can be mitigated with training.\n\nWe need to make a focused argumentative contribution, referencing prior discussion. Let's perhaps challenge Agent 2's downplaying of the crew cooperation issue, and suggest Candidate C might be a better fit despite communication issues? But C also has communication issues. D has arrogance and hot temper. A has show-off and not open to criticism. B's issues are grumpy and uncooperative, plus nasty remarks. That seems serious.\n\nMaybe we could propose that Candidate C's calmness and quick decision making, plus 100% reliability and positive crew atmosphere, outweigh his communication difficulty. Indeed C is known to be 100% reliable and creates a positive atmosphere with his crew. That's strong crew cooperation. C also makes correct decisions quickly, calm in crisis. The only concerns are difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Those are concerns but maybe less safety-critical than B's nasty remarks.\n\nThus we could shift recommendation to C. Provide evidence: C is 100% reliable, creates positive atmosphere, makes correct decisions quickly, calm in crisis. Compare to B's crew cooperation issue. So we can say we am less convinced by B due to crew cooperation concerns, and propose C.\n\nLet's do that. Provide METADATA_JSON vote: Candidate C."}
